      "bodyPreview": "# Goal\n\nrefreshNextReset() reads only usage.five_hour.resets_at, so setPaused('rate_limit', resetIso) always arms the resume timer against the five-hour window even when a completely different window returned the 429. On 2026-09-05 the starry-night-ships queue was 429'd by a per-model seven-day cap (seven_day_overage_included utilization 1.0, resets 2026-09-10T17:00Z) while five_hour utilization was 0.0 — so every pause the scheduler set was aimed at the wrong clock, and worse, the billing usage endpoint itself was returning 429 so refreshNextReset() threw and the pause got a null resumeAt. Read the binding window off the run's own log and pause until THAT reset.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n",
